.TH ADTOOL 1 "2026-09-18" "adtool 1.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adtool \- read and administer Active Directory over Kerberos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adtool user
.RI [ pattern ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B adtool group
.RI [ pattern ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B adtool computer
.RI [ pattern ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B adtool password policy
.br
.B adtool whoami
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adtool
queries Active Directory using the current Kerberos ticket and renders aligned
tables, CSV, or JSON. It can also reset passwords, disable accounts, and unlock
accounts over a sealed GSSAPI connection.
.SH USER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-g , " --groups"
Show nested group membership.
.TP
.BR \-c , " --count" [=KEY]
Count by department, title, OU, or status.
.TP
.BI --dept " NAME"
Filter by department prefix.
.TP
.BI --title " NAME"
Filter by title prefix.
.TP
.BI --expiring " DAYS"
Show passwords expiring within the given number of days.
.TP
.BI --stale " DAYS"
Show accounts with no recent logon.
.TP
.B --locked
Show accounts currently locked by Active Directory.
.TP
.BR --csv , " --json"
Produce machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR --reset , " --lock" , " --unlock"
Perform the selected action on an exact login after confirmation.
.SH GROUP OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m , " --members"
Show nested members.
.TP
.BR \-c , " --count"
Count groups by OU.
.SH COMPUTER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s , " --servers"
Show only server operating systems.
.TP
.BR \-w , " --workstations"
Show only non-server systems.
.TP
.BR \-c , " --count" [=KEY]
Count by operating system, version, or OU.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration file is
.IR ~/.config/adtool/config .
Set
.B AD_CONFIG
to use another path. Environment variables override values read from the file.
.TP
.B AD_LDAP_URI
LDAP URI of a domain controller.
.TP
.B AD_BASE_DN
Active Directory search base.
.TP
.B AD_KINIT_PRINCIPAL
Principal suggested when no Kerberos ticket exists.
.TP
.B AD_LOCKOUT_MINUTES
Fallback lockout duration for controllers that do not return their computed
lockout state. Zero means accounts remain locked until explicitly unlocked.
.SH SECURITY
Reads use GSSAPI authentication. Writes require a sealed GSSAPI session with a
minimum security strength factor of 128. Passwords are read without terminal
echo and are not stored in files or command-line arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A non-zero status indicates invalid input, no matching
objects, a missing Kerberos ticket, or an LDAP failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/adtool/config
Per-user configuration.
